# Windows batch files must keep CRLF line endings. cmd.exe parses an
# LF-only .bat unreliably: it drops the first characters of some lines,
# producing errors like "'tlocal' is not recognized as an internal or
# external command" from a `setlocal` it mangled. Without this rule,
# core.autocrlf decides per clone and the scripts break on some machines
# and not others.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts run inside the Linux Postgres container (docker/) and must
# keep LF, whatever the checkout platform does.
*.sh text eol=lf
